WEBVTT

00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:12.700
Looks like the whole town's in Christmas mode.

00:00:15.260 --> 00:00:17.020
Christmas means...

00:00:17.790 --> 00:00:19.870
You-know-what, right?

00:00:21.050 --> 00:00:23.580
Special Christmas sales!

00:00:25.550 --> 00:00:29.340
I found some new shopping buddies recently.

00:00:31.300 --> 00:00:33.180
I know they're all excited, too...

00:00:33.180 --> 00:00:34.300
Listen, you!

00:00:34.680 --> 00:00:38.000
Can't you act more like a normal high school girl?!

00:00:54.320 --> 00:00:56.070
Incredible! Did you see that?

00:00:56.070 --> 00:00:56.910
I can't believe it!

00:00:56.910 --> 00:00:58.370
What's all the fuss about?
I can't believe it!

00:00:58.370 --> 00:00:59.200
What's all the fuss about?

00:01:17.180 --> 00:01:19.380
Ugh...

00:01:20.040 --> 00:01:21.310
So tired...

00:01:24.640 --> 00:01:27.980
What?!

00:03:03.160 --> 00:03:05.490
Mornings are such a drag.

00:03:07.430 --> 00:03:09.540
I wanna go home already.

00:03:09.540 --> 00:03:12.100
Whoa, hang on a second!

00:03:12.680 --> 00:03:16.280
You didn't have to change <i>that</i> radically
to look like a high school girl!

00:03:16.780 --> 00:03:19.300
I mean, I know that's what I said yesterday, but...

00:03:19.640 --> 00:03:20.590
Huh?

00:03:20.590 --> 00:03:23.400
And what's with that outfit?

00:03:23.400 --> 00:03:25.470
What decade are you from?

00:03:25.470 --> 00:03:26.900
Who are you?

00:03:29.200 --> 00:03:30.810
Ugh, gag me with a spoon.

00:03:31.560 --> 00:03:32.860
Gag me with...

00:03:32.860 --> 00:03:34.720
It's gal-speak.

00:03:35.760 --> 00:03:36.820
Wait!

00:03:36.820 --> 00:03:40.700
I-I'm sorry! I can explain...

00:03:41.500 --> 00:03:42.620
Amami?

00:03:42.620 --> 00:03:44.330
Are you back to normal?

00:03:52.990 --> 00:03:55.630
Y'all are annoying as hell, you know?

00:03:55.630 --> 00:03:57.010
Who are you?!

00:04:02.790 --> 00:04:03.560
It...

00:04:04.340 --> 00:04:07.900
It's an endangered species!

00:04:16.610 --> 00:04:19.480
So, what happened?

00:04:19.480 --> 00:04:20.500
Well...

00:04:22.500 --> 00:04:24.300
On my way home yesterday...

00:04:33.330 --> 00:04:35.380
Act like a normal high school girl...

00:04:35.920 --> 00:04:37.640
But how should I do that?

00:04:37.640 --> 00:04:39.760
Something on your mind?

00:04:49.640 --> 00:04:53.690
If you're buggin', I can totally help. You dig?

00:04:53.950 --> 00:04:55.690
"Buggin'"?

00:04:55.690 --> 00:04:57.190
"You dig"?

00:04:57.190 --> 00:05:00.940
Wh-What?!

00:05:02.080 --> 00:05:06.070
S-So I asked her for advice.

00:05:07.660 --> 00:05:09.200
And she said...

00:05:09.200 --> 00:05:11.780
You wanna be like a normal high school girl?

00:05:11.780 --> 00:05:15.500
I'm on it, you dig?

00:05:15.860 --> 00:05:17.380
Really?

00:05:17.380 --> 00:05:20.510
In exchange, how about you lend me your body

00:05:20.780 --> 00:05:24.180
so my soul can pass on?

00:05:24.820 --> 00:05:26.510
Whoa!

00:05:26.790 --> 00:05:29.560
That's obviously dangerous!

00:05:30.060 --> 00:05:31.890
Y-You think so?

00:05:32.180 --> 00:05:34.390
Like, totally. You dig?

00:05:35.480 --> 00:05:37.390
You just wanted to say that.

00:05:40.230 --> 00:05:44.930
So I'm gonna borrow this girl's body for a while.

00:05:44.930 --> 00:05:46.900
Be cool, 'kay?

00:05:46.900 --> 00:05:50.910
This isn't what I meant by
acting like a high school girl!

00:05:51.280 --> 00:05:52.800
Get out of there!

00:05:53.270 --> 00:05:54.620
As if.

00:05:56.660 --> 00:05:59.050
Get back here!

00:05:59.050 --> 00:06:02.790
Oh, well. It's not like she's
been completely possessed.

00:06:02.790 --> 00:06:05.630
Once her soul passes on,
Amami will go back to normal, right?

00:06:05.630 --> 00:06:07.600
But how is she going to do that?

00:06:09.370 --> 00:06:10.570
Why, you...

00:06:12.010 --> 00:06:14.310
There's someone I wanna meet on Christmas!

00:06:14.790 --> 00:06:16.480
I can stay that long, right?

00:06:20.320 --> 00:06:23.570
A girl wants to meet someone on Christmas...

00:06:23.890 --> 00:06:25.450
That can only mean...

00:06:25.720 --> 00:06:27.950
She had a boyfriend!

00:06:27.950 --> 00:06:30.020
That's why she needs a body!

00:06:30.020 --> 00:06:33.960
No—

00:06:33.960 --> 00:06:35.200
E-Everyone calm down!
No!

00:06:35.200 --> 00:06:36.380
E-Everyone calm down!

00:06:46.060 --> 00:06:48.640
That includes you, roll-call samurai!

00:07:05.270 --> 00:07:06.570
Get lost!

00:07:06.570 --> 00:07:10.010
I'm keeping an eye on you!
We have a responsibility here.

00:07:10.480 --> 00:07:15.400
You think Inoue can keep that up until Christmas?

00:07:15.400 --> 00:07:17.380
Well, she may be weird,

00:07:17.380 --> 00:07:20.210
but she's not using Amami's
body to do anything bad...

00:07:24.670 --> 00:07:26.600
And... post.

00:07:26.600 --> 00:07:31.000
Your blog really makes the existence
of ghosts feel like a part of life, Uehara.

00:07:31.000 --> 00:07:32.140
You think so?

00:07:32.140 --> 00:07:35.280
It's important to bring information to the people!

00:07:38.630 --> 00:07:39.230
Wow.

00:07:39.580 --> 00:07:41.980
You're like a real journalist.

00:07:41.980 --> 00:07:43.910
Way to go, reporter Uehara!

00:07:43.910 --> 00:07:46.000
Let me get a shot of you!

00:07:46.000 --> 00:07:47.340
Kidding, kidding.

00:07:48.800 --> 00:07:49.490
Huh?

00:07:50.460 --> 00:07:52.280
Huh? Eh?

00:07:52.980 --> 00:07:53.630
What?

00:07:55.300 --> 00:07:56.740
Uehara?

00:07:56.740 --> 00:08:00.250
Wow, I've never seen you
make a face like this, Uehara!

00:08:14.600 --> 00:08:17.520
She smashed my phone...

00:08:17.850 --> 00:08:20.960
But why did Uehara look like that?

00:08:25.270 --> 00:08:29.130
Both her parents are journalists.

00:08:30.260 --> 00:08:31.570
Journalists?

00:08:31.570 --> 00:08:32.560
Yeah.

00:08:33.600 --> 00:08:36.140
So I guess she... you know...

00:08:36.790 --> 00:08:40.670
She was happy to be praised
for something she got from them.

00:08:41.080 --> 00:08:43.560
Oh, she was just being bashful?

00:08:43.560 --> 00:08:46.100
That's some extreme bashfulness...

00:08:49.370 --> 00:08:52.500
What, she's bragging about her parents?

00:08:52.940 --> 00:08:54.760
Gag me with a spoon.

00:08:55.120 --> 00:08:56.880
She wasn't bragging...

00:08:56.880 --> 00:09:00.400
Who cares about parents, anyway?

00:09:01.060 --> 00:09:03.390
Parents suck.

00:09:03.390 --> 00:09:07.410
Do-Don't say that! Parents are precious!

00:09:07.410 --> 00:09:08.360
And so are grandm—

00:09:08.360 --> 00:09:09.640
I don't get it.

00:09:09.640 --> 00:09:12.460
Well, figure it out!

00:09:12.460 --> 00:09:14.160
Whatever...

00:09:36.330 --> 00:09:37.630
First one there wins!

00:09:37.630 --> 00:09:39.120
Hey, wait for me!

00:09:39.120 --> 00:09:40.930
C'mon, hurry up!

00:09:43.060 --> 00:09:46.380
<i>Man, what's her deal, anyway?</i>

00:09:47.310 --> 00:09:48.350
Honestly...

00:09:50.820 --> 00:09:52.050
Huh? What is it?

00:09:52.050 --> 00:09:53.200
Shush!

00:09:59.430 --> 00:10:01.370
I just happened to spot her.

00:10:01.370 --> 00:10:03.790
And I smell a big scoop.

00:10:03.790 --> 00:10:06.290
<i>She's definitely a journalist.</i>

00:10:12.110 --> 00:10:13.740
What's she doing?

00:10:15.330 --> 00:10:16.350
<i>No way...</i>

00:10:16.750 --> 00:10:18.980
<i>Is she breaking into empty houses?!</i>

00:10:18.980 --> 00:10:23.610
<i>Or maybe scamming poor,
lonely old ladies over the phone?!</i>

00:10:31.150 --> 00:10:33.060
You can't do that!

00:10:33.060 --> 00:10:34.110
Inoue!

00:10:35.930 --> 00:10:38.860
Stop!

00:10:42.240 --> 00:10:43.200
Hey!

00:10:46.440 --> 00:10:48.250
I-I won't let you do it!

00:10:48.680 --> 00:10:51.140
It's just too cruel!

00:10:51.140 --> 00:10:54.040
Huh?! You're not making any sense!

00:10:55.330 --> 00:10:56.780
Hey. Here.

00:11:00.830 --> 00:11:02.200
An anonymous message?

00:11:03.140 --> 00:11:04.770
It's just a normal letter!

00:11:05.270 --> 00:11:06.150
Seriously!

00:11:10.440 --> 00:11:13.780
You were just leaving a letter
for the person you want to meet?

00:11:14.150 --> 00:11:17.670
I don't have a clue what
you were so suspicious of.

00:11:17.670 --> 00:11:20.060
You <i>were</i> kind of sneaking around, though.

00:11:20.060 --> 00:11:23.620
Like you can talk.
You've been sneaking pictures of me.

00:11:24.720 --> 00:11:29.070
Oh, is that how your parents get pictures, too?

00:11:29.070 --> 00:11:32.130
Trying to do what they do and make them proud?

00:11:32.130 --> 00:11:32.790
Huh?!

00:11:34.020 --> 00:11:34.620
H-Hey...

00:11:34.620 --> 00:11:35.510
Oh, my!

00:11:35.510 --> 00:11:37.300
Hibiki, there you are!

00:11:40.570 --> 00:11:42.530
What are you doing here?

00:11:43.120 --> 00:11:44.610
I'm, uh...

00:11:44.610 --> 00:11:46.470
Well, this is perfect.

00:11:46.470 --> 00:11:48.210
A sale's about to start!

00:11:48.210 --> 00:11:50.150
Sale? Wha— Let me go!

00:12:03.080 --> 00:12:06.820
Never underestimate the power of homemakers...

00:12:07.330 --> 00:12:11.410
They say you can't raise kids
without lots of stamina.

00:12:11.930 --> 00:12:15.510
Yeah, keeping an eye on them is a tough job.

00:12:15.510 --> 00:12:18.290
They'll run into the street
without a second thought.

00:12:21.730 --> 00:12:23.730
Yuuki!

00:12:23.730 --> 00:12:25.410
Can't get me now!

00:12:25.410 --> 00:12:28.800
Then they use the red light to escape. It's infuriating.

00:12:28.800 --> 00:12:32.700
I've heard other mothers talk about that.

00:12:33.150 --> 00:12:37.160
One mother told me that
was her child's specialty,

00:12:37.160 --> 00:12:38.970
though it was a long time ago.

00:12:41.800 --> 00:12:47.570
Mothers remember all sorts of
things about raising their children.

00:12:48.580 --> 00:12:49.650
Amami...

00:12:50.200 --> 00:12:51.580
There you are!

00:12:54.180 --> 00:12:57.670
Hibiki, here you go.

00:12:57.670 --> 00:13:01.610
It's the beef and potato stew
recipe I promised to give you.

00:13:04.300 --> 00:13:06.210
Thank you!

00:13:08.090 --> 00:13:11.720
I'm sorry. This recipe serves three.

00:13:11.720 --> 00:13:13.790
It's just me and my husband at home,

00:13:13.790 --> 00:13:16.070
but I always end up making extra.

00:13:17.550 --> 00:13:19.520
<i>Just you and your husband?</i>

00:13:19.520 --> 00:13:21.280
<i>Serves three?</i>

00:13:29.400 --> 00:13:30.310
Huh?

00:13:30.800 --> 00:13:34.990
You know, she's been pretty quiet for a while now.

00:13:35.560 --> 00:13:37.460
You think she's passed on?

00:13:38.920 --> 00:13:40.650
As if.

00:13:40.650 --> 00:13:41.840
She's back!

00:13:42.320 --> 00:13:44.620
Wh-Why were you so quiet?

00:13:44.620 --> 00:13:47.940
Ain't any of your business.

00:13:49.190 --> 00:13:51.590
Ah, it's probably my fault.

00:13:54.580 --> 00:13:59.950
You were saying how it pissed you off
that I took pride in acting like my parents.

00:13:59.950 --> 00:14:02.210
I-I didn't say it pissed me off...

00:14:03.320 --> 00:14:07.490
It's just gross for people your age
to be so close with their parents.

00:14:08.620 --> 00:14:10.490
We're not close or anything.

00:14:10.890 --> 00:14:15.380
My parents are so busy,
they're almost never home.

00:14:19.640 --> 00:14:20.610
Um...

00:14:21.260 --> 00:14:23.290
It's better without them, though, isn't it?

00:14:23.670 --> 00:14:28.050
You can relax and go nuts
with your friends all the time!

00:14:29.130 --> 00:14:31.260
Where'd that come from?

00:14:32.590 --> 00:14:35.760
Wait, are you trying to make me feel better?

00:14:36.080 --> 00:14:40.250
M-Make you feel better?
I have no idea what you mean!

00:14:40.250 --> 00:14:42.810
It's nothing like that, okay?!

00:14:43.360 --> 00:14:45.770
You're actually very...

00:14:46.300 --> 00:14:49.780
I-I'm telling you, I'm not!

00:14:52.540 --> 00:14:54.530
She told you that?

00:14:54.940 --> 00:14:59.040
Things have been like that
at Uehara's for ages now.

00:14:59.430 --> 00:15:02.390
It's not something outsiders
like us can do anything about.

00:15:02.390 --> 00:15:03.270
But...

00:15:03.270 --> 00:15:08.070
Why bother, anyway? They'd just
get on your case for butting in.

00:15:08.070 --> 00:15:10.500
You're still saying stuff like that?

00:15:11.140 --> 00:15:12.180
But...

00:15:12.800 --> 00:15:17.100
Her parents are coming home for Christmas.

00:15:18.860 --> 00:15:22.370
Really? That's great!

00:15:24.250 --> 00:15:26.730
Oh, good, you're all here.

00:15:27.030 --> 00:15:28.740
Morning, Uehara!

00:15:28.740 --> 00:15:33.040
You've all kept your schedules
clear for Christmas, right?

00:15:33.960 --> 00:15:36.880
We've gotta have a Christmas party.

00:15:37.380 --> 00:15:40.830
Oh, but only after the gal ghost's
soul has passed on, of course.

00:15:41.900 --> 00:15:42.750
But...

00:15:43.160 --> 00:15:45.620
Aren't your parents coming home?

00:15:46.200 --> 00:15:48.510
Oh, don't worry about them.

00:15:48.510 --> 00:15:51.020
It probably won't work out, just like always.

00:15:52.510 --> 00:15:54.760
"Something came up. We can't make it."

00:15:55.110 --> 00:15:58.080
That's just the line of work they're in.

00:15:58.080 --> 00:16:02.140
Hey, don't even worry about your parents!

00:16:02.140 --> 00:16:05.850
Yeah, you're right.
It'll be more fun with friends, anyway.

00:16:05.850 --> 00:16:08.150
Yeah! Like, totally!

00:16:08.620 --> 00:16:10.650
You really do get it!

00:16:28.170 --> 00:16:30.370
So the big day is finally here.

00:16:30.370 --> 00:16:32.280
Is this really gonna work?

00:16:32.280 --> 00:16:35.990
She said she'd be satisfied
once she passed on her message.

00:16:35.990 --> 00:16:37.280
Someone's coming.

00:16:51.940 --> 00:16:55.530
H-Hibiki, did you deliver this?

00:17:02.620 --> 00:17:04.310
You jerk!

00:17:07.630 --> 00:17:10.540
Why can't you make up your
damn mind, you meddling witch?!

00:17:11.030 --> 00:17:14.550
Hurry up and have a second one already,
you saggy old hag!

00:17:18.550 --> 00:17:21.060
She chewed her out and then ran away...

00:17:21.060 --> 00:17:23.920
Wh-What the hell is she thinking?!

00:17:23.920 --> 00:17:24.860
Wait.

00:17:25.560 --> 00:17:27.640
I think that might be her...

00:17:36.780 --> 00:17:39.320
I always end up making extra...

00:17:43.370 --> 00:17:44.880
I'm sorry.

00:17:46.550 --> 00:17:50.580
Don't apologize. That's her portion.

00:17:51.320 --> 00:17:54.340
For a worthless daughter like me...

00:17:58.970 --> 00:18:01.850
Why would you hold on to this for over ten years?

00:18:02.790 --> 00:18:06.330
So the one you wanted to see was your mother.

00:18:09.600 --> 00:18:13.940
I-I was just sick of watching her
still clinging to the past.

00:18:15.380 --> 00:18:21.630
Mothers never forget their memories
of raising their children.

00:18:26.650 --> 00:18:30.320
So I'm sure yours won't forget you, either.

00:18:32.300 --> 00:18:34.380
Sorry for all the trouble.

00:18:36.680 --> 00:18:38.740
I'm outta here now, for real.

00:18:39.220 --> 00:18:40.220
Wait!

00:18:42.220 --> 00:18:43.220
What?!

00:18:46.200 --> 00:18:47.270
Wait!

00:19:28.470 --> 00:19:33.190
You need to write a more proper letter,

00:19:33.190 --> 00:19:35.540
or they're going to laugh at you up in heaven.

00:19:43.750 --> 00:19:45.030
I'm sorry...

00:19:46.880 --> 00:19:49.330
I'm sorry I died first!

00:19:49.920 --> 00:19:52.650
I'm sorry I couldn't give anything back to you!

00:19:52.650 --> 00:19:53.570
Silly...

00:19:55.280 --> 00:19:57.930
I'm sorry I was such an awful daughter...

00:19:57.930 --> 00:19:59.340
How can you say that?

00:19:59.340 --> 00:20:04.340
I'm sorry... I'm sorry...

00:20:15.750 --> 00:20:18.360
Thank you, Mom.

00:20:21.650 --> 00:20:22.990
That's wonderful.

00:20:23.380 --> 00:20:25.980
So she finally passed on?

00:20:25.980 --> 00:20:27.520
Now all that's left is...

00:20:29.170 --> 00:20:32.830
C-Coward... It's just not fair...

00:20:32.830 --> 00:20:35.260
Hey, broken dam.

00:20:35.260 --> 00:20:37.460
Will you turn off the waterworks already?

00:20:37.460 --> 00:20:41.420
Yeah! It's Christmas. Let's celebrate!

00:20:43.380 --> 00:20:45.200
Yay!

00:20:47.390 --> 00:20:49.210
She didn't pass on?

00:20:50.190 --> 00:20:54.310
Yeah, well, there's still something bugging me.

00:21:00.540 --> 00:21:02.300
What are <i>you</i> doing?

00:21:03.450 --> 00:21:06.960
Don't you have people waiting for you?

00:21:09.250 --> 00:21:10.780
It's your turn now.

00:21:29.650 --> 00:21:33.460
I understand how you feel.

00:22:05.610 --> 00:22:06.880
I'm home.

00:23:41.980 --> 00:23:43.100
I'm Ogawa Makoto!

00:23:43.690 --> 00:23:46.470
I once said, "Aren't rotting things great?"

00:23:46.470 --> 00:23:49.110
And a girl invited me to join the manga club.

00:23:49.110 --> 00:23:50.610
What was that about?

00:23:50.610 --> 00:23:53.580
I can't believe the year's already over.

00:23:53.580 --> 00:23:56.110
I wonder what next year will bring...

00:23:56.110 --> 00:24:00.710
Hey, why do the roll-call samurai
and the others look so down?

00:24:01.110 --> 00:24:04.790
Next time on Re-Kan!:
"A Busy New Year."

00:24:05.340 --> 00:24:08.130
I wonder if I'll meet a nice
hunk of rotting flesh next year?
